---
name: "Our Work"
title: "Genetic screening programmes in India | Lightening Lives"
description: "Genetic screening in nine states and Delhi, accounts from the field, patents granted in India and Japan, and where we have presented our work."
label: Our work
kicker: "Real-world impact and evidence"
mosaic: true
h1: 'In the field. In the lab. <span class="h-mark">In print.</span>'
lead: "Public health screening across India's underserved belts, hands-on laboratory capacity building, and the scientific evidence behind every LitLife™ test."
proof:
  - { icon: "map-pin", text: "15 sites, 9 states and Delhi" }
  - { icon: "award", text: "Patents granted in India and Japan" }
  - { icon: "badge-check", text: "ICMR approved" }
closing:
  h2: 'Want to run a screening programme <span class="h-mark">like these?</span>'
  body: "Tell us the community, the condition and the institution you work with. We help design, run and monitor it."
  solid: { text: "Talk to us about programmes and CSR", who: "programme" }
  line: { text: "Partner with us: labs and hospitals", href: "/partner-with-us/#laboratories" }
pillars:
  - { icon: "users", name: "In the community", line: "screening and awareness camps", tag: "For public health and CSR programmes", body: "A camp explains the condition and how it is passed on, assesses nutrition, and collects a finger-prick dried blood spot from every participant, with no cold chain." }
  - { icon: "baby", name: "Newborn screening", line: "a diagnosis from day one", tag: "Rajasthan and Maharashtra", place: true, body: "LitLife™-SCA screens newborns for sickle cell from a heel-prick spot, without the 72-hour wait or the fetal haemoglobin interference of older tests." }
  - { icon: "flask-conical", name: "In the laboratory", line: "high-throughput batches", tag: "For hospitals and diagnostic chains", body: "Regional and hospital laboratories process dozens of cards in a single run, with screening and molecular confirmation on the same day." }
  - { icon: "graduation-cap", name: "Capacity building", line: "training the people who run the tests", tag: "For laboratories and health workers", body: "Hands-on workshops for technicians on direct-DBS PCR and gel reading, and for health workers on barcoded card collection, so partners run LitLife™ independently." }
---
{#- Our work (content file 5.7; five sections since 25 October 2026, the reviewer's site map, 3.1;
    since the client review of 27 October 2026, plan 2026-11-05 Task 5: the four pillars first, Odisha
    on the map as a field account, each account's outcome in sight, patents folded into #media): the
    company's record. The opening (no numbers strip until people screened is confirmed); recent work
    in photographs (#recent, src/site/_data/gallery.json, a mosaic, all at once); the field
    programmes (#field: the poster's table by state, never by town, and three accounts from the field
    whose second half opens in place); patents (#publications, the patents first; papers wait for
    the company's list); conferences and media (#media: the poster first, opened full size, and the
    YouTube channel). One map
    on the site, the home page's. The table comes from src/site/_data/sites.json, grouped by state in
    work.states' order. -#}
{%- from "picture.njk" import picture with context %}
{%- set arrow = '<svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M1 6h15M11 1l5 5-5 5"/></svg>' %}

  <!-- 1. The four ways the work happens: one panel, four ruled columns -->
  <section id="pillars" class="section" aria-labelledby="pillars-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="pillars-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Where screening has to reach. <span class="h-mark">How we make it happen.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">From remote tribal villages to district molecular laboratories, we work with state governments, CSR foundations, NGOs and hospitals to build self-sustaining diagnostic programmes.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="pillars mt-12">
        {%- for p in pillars %}
        <li class="pillar">
          <h3><span class="pillar-name">{% icon p.icon %}{{ p.name }}:</span> <span class="pillar-line">{{ p.line }}</span></h3>
          <p class="pillar-body">{{ p.body }}</p>
          <p class="pillar-tag">{% icon "map-pin" if p.place else "building-2" %}<span>{{ p.tag }}</span></p>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Recent work: the photographs, sliding by themselves; a slide may carry a title, words and a link -->
  <section id="recent" class="section on-mist gallery-band" aria-labelledby="recent-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="recent-h" class="sr-only">Recent work, in photographs</h2>
      {#- The photographs as a mosaic (26 October 2026; the user found the slideshow's progress bars,
          pause and arrows "old and not modern", and many more photographs are to come). In sets of
          six: a feature over two rows, two beside it, three under them; every other set mirrored; a
          last set short of six is set as one even row. Words, a story's or a caption, sit under their
          photograph, never over it. Each photograph opens large in the viewer (main.js, PhotoSwipe);
          without script its link opens the largest file. Past the first twelve the rest wait behind
          "Show more photographs" (all are in the page; without script all show). Each is sized to its
          slot; a photograph that comes into view develops once (motion.js). -#}
      {%- set n = gallery.slides | length %}
      {%- set full = (n / 6) | int * 6 %}
      {%- set tail = n - full %}
      {%- set sizes = {
        "slot-1": "(min-width: 64rem) 52rem, 100vw",
        "slot-2": "(min-width: 64rem) 26rem, (min-width: 40rem) 50vw, 100vw",
        "slot-3": "(min-width: 64rem) 26rem, (min-width: 40rem) 50vw, 100vw",
        "slot-4": "(min-width: 64rem) 33rem, (min-width: 40rem) 50vw, 100vw",
        "slot-5": "(min-width: 64rem) 20rem, 100vw",
        "slot-6": "(min-width: 64rem) 26rem, (min-width: 40rem) 50vw, 100vw",
        "slot-tail": "(min-width: 64rem) 40rem, (min-width: 40rem) 50vw, 100vw"
      } %}
      <ul class="mosaic" data-mosaic>
        {%- for slide in gallery.slides %}
        {%- set i = loop.index0 %}
        {%- if i < full %}{% set slot = "slot-" + (i % 6 + 1) %}{% set mirror = ((i / 6) | int) % 2 == 1 %}{% else %}{% set slot = "slot-tail" %}{% set mirror = false %}{% endif %}
        {%- set entry = images[slide.image] %}
        {%- set big = entry.widths | last %}
        <li class="tile {{ slot }}{{ ' is-mirror' if mirror }}{{ ' tail-' + tail if slot == 'slot-tail' }}{% if slide.title %} tile-story{% else %} tile-photo{% endif %}" data-mosaic-tile>
          <a class="tile-pic" href="/assets/img/{{ slide.image }}-{{ big }}.webp" data-pswp-width="{{ big }}" data-pswp-height="{{ (entry.height * big / entry.widths[0]) | round }}" data-pswp-srcset="{% for w in entry.widths %}/assets/img/{{ slide.image }}-{{ w }}.webp {{ w }}w{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}" data-pswp-cropped="true">{{ picture(slide.image, slide.alt, sizes[slot], { class: "tile-img", eager: i < 3 }) }}<span class="tile-open" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "maximize-2" %}</span></a>
          {%- if not slide.title %}
          <p class="tile-caption">{% icon slide.icon or "camera" %}<span>{{ slide.caption }}</span></p>
          {%- else %}
          <div class="tile-words">
            <p class="tile-kind">{% icon slide.icon or "camera" %}<span>{{ slide.kind }}</span></p>
            <h3>{{ slide.title }}</h3>
            {%- if slide.body %}<p class="tile-body">{{ slide.body }}</p>{% endif %}
            {%- if slide.link %}<a class="link" href="{{ slide.link.href }}">{{ slide.link.text }} {{ arrow | safe }}</a>{% endif %}
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      {%- if n > 12 %}
      <p class="mosaic-more" data-mosaic-more hidden><button type="button" class="btn btn-line">{% icon "images" %}<span>Show more photographs</span> <small data-mosaic-left></small></button></p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Field programmes: the table by state, then the accounts -->
  <section id="field" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="field-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="field-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Field programmes. <span class="h-mark">Where we have screened, state by state.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Fifteen sites in nine states and Delhi, concentrated in the sickle cell and thalassaemia belt of central and western India, where the need is greatest.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fieldmap mt-12" id="sites" data-fieldmap>
        <div class="fieldmap-stage">
          <svg class="fieldmap-svg" viewBox="{{ fieldmap.viewBox }}" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            {#- A field account's state (no site of ours there) is hatched, not filled: the key says so. #}
            <defs><pattern id="fm-hatch" width="1.6" height="1.6" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(45)"><rect class="fm-hatch-ground" width="1.6" height="1.6"/><rect class="fm-hatch-line" width="0.55" height="1.6"/></pattern></defs>
            {%- for st in fieldmap.states %}
            <path class="fm-state{% if st.worked %} is-worked{% elif st.account %} is-account{% endif %}" d="{{ st.d }}"{% if st.worked or st.account %} data-fm-state="{{ st.id }}"{% endif %}/>
            {%- endfor %}
          </svg>
          <ul class="fieldmap-pins" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- for st in fieldmap.picks %}
            <li style="left: {{ st.pin.left }}%; top: {{ st.pin.top }}%" data-fm-pin="{{ st.id }}"{% if st.account %} class="is-account"{% endif %}>{% if st.account %}<i class="fm-ring">{% icon "book-open" %}</i>{% else %}<img src="/assets/logo/lightening-lives-emblem.svg" alt="" width="60" height="60">{% endif %}<span>{{ st.name }}</span></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
          <ul class="fieldmap-key" aria-hidden="true">
            <li><i class="is-site"></i>Screening sites</li>
            <li><i class="is-account"></i>Field account</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="fieldmap-side">
          <p class="fieldmap-hint">{% icon "mouse-pointer-click" %}<span>Choose a state, on the map or below.</span></p>
          <ul class="fieldmap-states">
            {%- for st in fieldmap.picks %}
            <li><button type="button" class="fm-chip{% if st.account %} is-account{% endif %}" data-fm-pick="{{ st.id }}" aria-controls="fm-panel-{{ st.id }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}">{% if st.account %}{% icon "book-open" %}{{ st.name }}{% else %}{{ st.name }} <small>{{ st.sites }}</small>{% endif %}</button></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
          {%- for st in fieldmap.picks %}
          <article class="fm-panel{% if st.account %} is-account{% endif %}" id="fm-panel-{{ st.id }}" data-fm-panel="{{ st.id }}" aria-labelledby="fm-h-{{ st.id }}">
            <header class="fm-panel-head">
              <h3 id="fm-h-{{ st.id }}">{{ st.name }}</h3>
              {%- if st.account %}
              <span class="fm-account">{% icon "book-open" %}Field account</span>
              {%- else %}
              <span class="fm-sites">{% icon "map-pin" %}{{ st.sites }} {{ "site" if st.sites == 1 else "sites" }}</span>
              {%- endif %}
            </header>
            {%- if st.line %}<p class="fm-line">{{ st.line }}</p>{% endif %}
            {%- if st.conditions.length %}
            <ul class="fm-screened">
              {%- for c in st.conditions %}
              <li><span class="fm-condition">{{ c.condition }}</span><span class="fm-kinds">{% for k in c.kinds %}<span class="fm-kind{% if k == 'Newborn' %} is-newborn{% endif %}">{% icon "baby" if k == "Newborn" else "users" %}{{ k }}</span>{% endfor %}</span></li>
              {%- endfor %}
            </ul>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- if st.stories.length %}
            <p class="fm-story">{% icon "book-open" %}<span>From the field: {% for story in st.stories %}<a class="link" href="#{{ story.id }}">{{ story.title }}</a>{% endfor %}</span></p>
            {%- endif %}
          </article>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sites-thanks">Source: Lightening Lives field records, {{ fieldmap.totals.sites }} sites in {{ fieldmap.totals.states }} states and Delhi. We thank the participating individuals, clinicians and frontline health workers at every site.</p>

      <h3 class="audience-h mt-16" id="accounts">From the field: when molecular diagnosis reaches the last mile</h3>
      <p class="field-note">Three accounts from our work with partner institutions, NGOs and government programmes. Identifying details have been left out to protect families.</p>
      <ul class="field-stories mt-6">
        {%- for story in fieldStories %}
        <li class="field-story" id="{{ story.id }}">
          <div class="field-story-head">
            <span class="icon-tile">{% icon story.icon %}</span>
            <span class="field-story-tags"><span>{% icon "map-pin" %}{{ story.state }}</span><span>{{ story.condition }}</span></span>
          </div>
          <h4>{{ story.title }}</h4>
          <p>{{ story.first }}</p>
          <div class="field-led">
            <p class="field-led-h">What it led to</p>
            <ul class="field-impact">
              {%- for line in story.impact %}
              <li>{% icon "arrow-right" %}<span>{{ line }}</span></li>
              {%- endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Conferences, publications and media: the poster, the patents, the channel -->
  <section id="media" class="section" aria-labelledby="media-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="media-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Conferences, publications and media. <span class="h-mark">Where we have presented.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Our patents, our poster to the haematology community, and talks and films from our work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="media mt-12">
        <a class="media-poster" href="/assets/img/work-fullposter-v9-1920.webp" aria-label="Open the poster full size">
          {{ picture("work-poster-v9", "The top of the poster: its title, A Novel Molecular Screening cum Confirmatory Kit for Sickle Cell Anemia and other Hemoglobinopathies, with the Lightening Lives logo and the REASSURED criteria.", "(min-width: 64rem) 46vw, 92vw", { class: "media-poster-img" }) }}
        </a>
        <div class="media-body">
          <span class="media-kind">{% icon "presentation" %}Poster, October 2026</span>
          <h3>A novel molecular screening cum confirmatory kit for sickle cell anaemia and other haemoglobinopathies</h3>
          <p>How LitLife™ meets the WHO REASSURED criteria, the six-step dried blood spot workflow, a comparison with HPLC and point-of-care tests, our hub-and-spoke model and field results from 15 sites.</p>
          <div class="media-act">
            <a class="btn btn-line" href="/assets/img/work-fullposter-v9-1920.webp">See the full poster</a>
          </div>
          <a class="media-channel" href="https://www.youtube.com/@LighteningLivesLLP" rel="noopener">
            <span class="media-channel-icon">{% brand "youtube" %}</span>
            <span><b>Our YouTube channel</b><small>Talks by Dr. Giriraj Ratan Chandak, laboratory demonstrations of the LitLife™ workflow, and films from our screening camps.</small></span>
            {% icon "arrow-up-right" %}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="patents-band mt-12">
        <div class="patents-head">
          <h3 class="audience-h">Patents</h3>
          <p class="patents-line">Protecting the direct dried blood spot amplification chemistry behind our tests.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="patents" id="patents">
          <li><span class="patent-flag">IN</span><div><h4>Patent granted in India</h4></div><span class="patent-state">Granted</span></li>
          <li><span class="patent-flag">JP</span><div><h4>Patent granted in Japan</h4></div><span class="patent-state">Granted</span></li>
          <li><span class="patent-flag">{% icon "globe" %}</span><div><h4>Globally published patent</h4></div><span class="patent-state is-published">Published</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- set articles = news.articles | sort(true, false, "date") %}
  {%- if articles.length %}
  <!-- In the news: newspaper and media coverage, newest first -->
  <section id="news" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="news-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="news-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">In the news. <span class="h-mark">What the press has written.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Newspaper and media coverage of our work and our tests.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="news-list mt-12">
        {%- for a in articles %}
        <li>
          <a class="news-item" href="{{ a.url }}" rel="noopener">
            <span class="news-outlet">{% icon "newspaper" %}{{ a.outlet }}{% if a.language %} <small>{{ a.language }}</small>{% endif %}</span>
            <span class="news-headline">{{ a.headline }}</span>
            {%- if a.excerpt %}<span class="news-excerpt">{{ a.excerpt }}</span>{% endif %}
            <span class="news-meta"><time datetime="{{ a.date }}">{{ a.date | newsDate }}</time><span class="news-read">Read the article {% icon "arrow-up-right" %}</span></span>
          </a>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}
